---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Concepts - Dasher">
  <h1>Concepts</h1>

  <p>Welcome to the Dasher concepts documentation. This section explains key concepts and principles behind Dasher's design and operation.</p>

  <div class="concept-grid">
    <section class="concept-card">
      <h2>Information Theory</h2>
      <p>Dasher is built on principles of information theory, using language models to predict the most likely next characters and allocate screen space accordingly.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="concept-card">
      <h2>Zooming Interface</h2>
      <p>Dasher uses a unique zooming interface where you navigate through a library of all possible text by steering toward your desired destination.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="concept-card">
      <h2>Language Models</h2>
      <p>Dasher's predictions are based on training texts that help it learn language patterns and adapt to your writing style over time.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="concept-card">
      <h2>Continuous Gestures</h2>
      <p>Unlike traditional keyboards that use discrete key presses, Dasher uses continuous pointing gestures for efficient text entry.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="concept-card">
      <h2>Accessibility</h2>
      <p>Dasher is designed to be accessible to users with various disabilities, supporting input methods like eye-tracking, head-tracking, and breath control.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="concept-card">
      <h2>Mode-Free Operation</h2>
      <p>Dasher eliminates the need to switch between writing and prediction modes, integrating word completion seamlessly into the writing process.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="learn-more">
    <h2>Learn More</h2>
    <p>For a detailed explanation of how Dasher works, see the <a href="/docs/getting-started/how-to/manual/part1/">Introduction</a> section of the Dasher Manual.</p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .concept-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .concept-card {
    background-color: var(--color-canvas-white);
    border: 2px solid var(--color-horizon-mint);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    transition: var(--transition-smooth);
  }

  .concept-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-target-coral);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  .concept-card h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--color-deep-ink);
  }

  .concept-card p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .learn-more {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    background-color: var(--color-horizon-mint);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }

  .learn-more h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--color-deep-ink);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  a:hover {
    color: var(--color-target-coral);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
